1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. d4 d6 4. Nf3 g6 5. Bc4 Nb6 6. Bb3 Bg7 7. a4 $5 {Entering extremly complicated variation with mutual chanses.} dxe5 8. a5 N6d7 {Accepting the chalange.After cautious} (8... Nd5 9. Nxe5 O-O 10. O-O c6 (10... c5 $6 11. Nxf7 $1 Kxf7 12. Qf3+ Kg8 13. Qxd5+ Qxd5 14. Bxd5+ e6 15. Be4 cxd4 16. Bg5 $14 {Nunn,J-Schroll,G/Vienna 1991}) (10... e6 11. Nf3 c5 12. c4 Nb4 13. Bg5 Bf6 14. Bxf6 Qxf6 15. Nc3 cxd4 16. Ne4 Qg7 17. c5 N8c6 $13 {½-½ Hracek,Z-Varga,Z/Odorheiu Secuiesc zt 1995}) 11. Nd2 Na6 12. Ndf3 f6 13. Nd3 Be6 14. Re1 Bf7 15. Qe2 Re8 16. Nf4 $14 {white gets very comfortable position in all variations; Mokry,K-Schroll,G/Vienna 1991}) 9. Bxf7+ $5 (9. dxe5 $6 Nxe5 10. Qxd8+ Kxd8 11. Ng5 Ke8 12. Nc3 h6 13. Nge4 Na6 $17 {Nicholson,J-Khmelnitsky,I/Spring op 1990}) 9... Kxf7 10. Ng5+ Kg8 11. Ne6 Qe8 12. Nxc7 {This line was formerly discredited because of a game in which black played 12...f7, but did not get enough for the exchange. Alburt's move is a significant improvement.} Qd8 $1 (12... Qf7 $6 13. Nxa8 exd4 14. O-O Na6 15. c3 h6 16. cxd4 Kh7 17. Na3 $14 {Lau,R-Posch,W/Jacques Lemans op16 1996}) 13. Nxa8 (13. Ne6 Qe8 14. Nc7 {½-½ Svidler,P-Khalifman,A/EUCup Gr5 1995}) 13... exd4 14. O-O (14. c3 $2 Nc5 15. cxd4 (15. b4 Ne4 16. Qb3+ e6 17. cxd4 Nc6 $1 { Dlugy.}) 15... Bxd4 16. O-O e5 17. Be3 Nba6 (17... Nc6 18. Bxd4 exd4 19. Qc2 Ne6 20. a6 Qd5 21. Nd2 Kg7 $36 {Cooper,L-Smith,G/Walsall 1992}) 18. Nc3 Bf5 19. Rc1 Kg7 20. Bxd4 Qxd4 21. b4 Nd3 22. Ne2 Qd7 $17 {Christiansen,L-Alburt,L/USA-ch m 1990}) 14... Nc6 15. c3 Nc5 16. b4 dxc3 $5 (16... Ne6 $2 17. Qb3 dxc3 18. Nxc3 $16 {Gubanov,A-Romanovich,L/Chigorin mem 1995}) 17. Qxd8+ Nxd8 18. bxc5 $6 {Critical position of the game.After white's last move black easily solves opening problems,so better was} (18. Ra3 $5 Ne4 19. Re1 c2 20. Nd2 Nxd2 21. Bxd2 Bf6 22. Nc7 $14 {with advantage.}) 18... c2 19. Nc3 Bxc3 20. Ra3 Bf6 21. Nc7 Nc6 22. Nd5 Kf7 $132 ({Another promising possibility was} 22... Bd4 $5 23. Be3 e5 24. Bxd4 exd4 25. Rc1 Bf5 26. g4 d3 $1 $13 {with unclear position.}) 23. Nxf6 exf6 24. f3 h5 {[%cal Gc8f5]} 25. h3 h4 $1 $15 {Ensuaring the square f5 for the bishop.} 26. Rf2 Bf5 27. a6 bxa6 (27... Rb8 $1) 28. Rxa6 Rc8 29. Kh2 Rc7 ({Deserved attention} 29... Bd3 30. Ra3 Bf5 31. Rd2 (31. Ra6) 31... a5 32. Rd6 Rc7 $15 {[%cal Gc6e5,Ge5d3] with better chanses.}) 30. Rd2 Ne5 31. Rdd6 Nd3 32. Rxf6+ Kg7 33. Bg5 Nxc5 $6 {After this move black finds himself on defensive,whie after} (33... c1=Q 34. Bxc1 Nxc1 35. Rfc6 Rxc6 36. Rxc6 Nb3 37. Rc7+ Kf6 $11 {black even has symbolical advantage.}) 34. Rac6 Rxc6 35. Rxc6 Nb3 36. Rc3 Nd4 37. Rc7+ Kf8 38. Rxa7 (38. Kg1 $5) 38... Ne2 {[%csl Rh2] Now white king can't get out of the corner.} 39. Rc7 $14 Kg8 40. Rc4 Kf7 41. Rxh4 {The only way to play for a win,but black easily holds this endgame.} c1=Q 42. Bxc1 Nxc1 43. g4 (43. Rc4 Ne2 $1 44. f4 Ke6 45. g4 Bd3 46. Rb4 Kd5 $11) 43... Be6 44. Rh7+ Kf6 45. h4 Ne2 46. Kg2 (46. h5 $6 g5 $11) 46... Ke5 47. Ra7 Nf4+ 48. Kg3 Ne2+ 49. Kf2 Nf4 50. Ra3 Kf6 51. Ra4 Nd5 52. Re4 Nc3 53. Re1 Nd5 54. Kg3 Kf7 55. Ra1 Kf6 56. Ra7 Ne3 57. Ra6 (57. Kf4 Ng2+ 58. Kg3 Ne3) 57... Nd5 58. Ra3 Kf7 59. Ra7+ Kf6 60. Ra5 Kf7 61. Ra6 Kf6 62. f4 Ne3 63. Kf3 Nxg4 $1 64. Rxe6+ Kxe6 65. Kxg4 Kf6 (65... Kf6 66. Kf3 Kf7 67. Ke4 Ke6 $11) 1/2-1/2

