1. d4 Nf6 2. Bg5 Ne4 3. Bf4 c5 4. f3 Qa5+ 5. c3 Nf6 6. Nd2 cxd4 7. Nb3 Qd8 (7... Qh5 8. cxd4 d5 9. g4 Qh4+ 10. Bg3 Qh6 11. h4 Nfd7 12. Rc1 Na6 13. Nh3 Qb6 14. e3 e6 15. a3 Be7 16. Bd3 Nf8 17. Rc3 Bd7 18. Qc1 Bb5 19. Bb1 Nd7 20. Nf4 Bd6 21. Kf2 Ba4 22. Nd2 {Salov,V-Polgar,J/Madrid 1995/CBM 47/[Stohl]/1-0 (85)}) 8. cxd4 g6 (8... d5 9. e3 e6 10. Rc1 Nc6 11. Bb5 Bd7 12. Ne2 Bb4+ 13. Kf2 Qb6 14. Bd3 O-O 15. g4 Rfe8 16. a3 Bf8 17. Bg5 Qd8 18. h4 e5 19. Nc3 Be6 20. dxe5 Nxe5 21. Bb5 Nc6 22. Nd4 Rc8 23. Qa4 {Hodgson,J-Babula,V/Delmenhorst GER 2000/The Week in Chess 272/0-1 (44)}) 9. e4 Bg7 10. Ne2 $146 (10. Bd3 O-O 11. Ne2 d6 12. Be3 (12. O-O Nc6 13. Be3 b6 14. Rc1 Bb7 15. Bb5 Rc8 16. d5 Ne5 17. Ned4 Rxc1 18. Qxc1 Qb8 19. Rf2 Rc8 20. Rc2 Rxc2 21. Qxc2 $16 {Adams,M-Georgiev,K/Las Palmas 1993/CBM 36/[Schussler]/1-0 (63)}) 12... Nc6 13. Qd2 a5 14. Rc1 a4 15. Na1 d5 16. e5 Nd7 17. h4 Qa5 18. h5 Qxd2+ 19. Kxd2 Nb6 20. h6 Bh8 21. Rc5 f6 22. f4 {½-½ Mikhalevski,V-Avrukh,B/Beersheba 1996/CBM 53 (43)}) 10... O-O 11. Nc3 d6 12. Be2 a6 13. O-O b5 14. a3 Nbd7 15. Qd2 Bb7 16. Be3 e6 17. Na2 Rb8 18. Na5 (18. Rac1 $5) 18... Ba8 19. Rac1 Qb6 20. Rc2 (20. b4 $1 {[%mdl 48] Much stronger was to fix the pawn structure, after} Rfc8 21. Nc3 d5 22. e5 Ne8 23. Nb3 $16 {[%csl Ra8,Gc5,Rg7] White has a clear advantage.}) 20... Rfc8 21. Rfc1 Rxc2 22. Rxc2 d5 23. e5 Ne8 24. Nc1 Bf8 25. Nd3 Qd8 26. Bg5 (26. b4 $5 Nb6 27. Nc5 Qc8 $14) 26... Qb6 27. Be3 Qd8 28. Bg5 Qb6 1/2-1/2

