1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Nxc6 Qf6 6. Qd2 dxc6 7. Nc3 Ne7 8. Qf4 Qe6 {Full information about this rare line you can find in my comments of the Nataf-Romanishin,1999/CBM74 See also Botsanin-Goldin,RUS-Cup9 CBM60} (8... Ng6 {is the main line}) 9. Bd3 O-O 10. O-O Ng6 11. Qg3 (11. Qg5 Qe5 12. Kh1 ({Nisipeanu played} 12. Qxe5 {See below.}) 12... Be6 13. Be3 Qxg5 14. Bxg5 f6 15. Bd2 Ne5 16. Be2 Rad8 17. Bf4 b5 18. f3 Rd7 19. Rad1 Bd4 20. Rd2 Rfd8 21. Bxe5 $2 Bxe5 22. Rxd7 Rxd7 $15 {0-1 Waldmann,G-Jankovic,A/Pula 1999/EXT 2000 (41)}) 11... Qe5 ({Another execution of the same idea was tried by Flear:} 11... Qd6 12. Bd2 (12. Ne2 f5 13. Nf4 fxe4 14. Nxg6 Qxg6 15. Qxg6 hxg6 16. Bxe4 Bf5 17. Bxf5 Rxf5 18. Be3 Bxe3 (18... Re8 $5 19. Rae1 Rfe5 20. Bd2 Re2 $1) 19. fxe3 Rd8 $11 {½-½ Baklan,V-Flear,G/1998-9 French Team Ch FRA 1999 (62)}) 12... f5 13. exf5 Qxg3 14. hxg3 Bxf5 15. Bxf5 Rxf5 16. Ne4 Bb6 17. Rfe1 Ne5 18. Be3 Nc4 19. Bxb6 axb6 20. b3 Nd6 21. a4 b5 22. a5 Re5 23. Nxd6 Rxe1+ 24. Rxe1 {½-½ Nunn,J-Flear,G/Hastings 1996/CBM 57 (24)}) 12. Qxe5 (12. Ne2 Qxg3 13. Nxg3 Be6 14. Ne2 (14. Be2 f6 15. Kh1 a5 16. f4 Bf7 17. Bd3 Rfe8 18. Bd2 a4 19. Nf5 Ne7 20. Nh4 Be6 21. Nf3 b5 22. h3 Rad8 23. f5 Bd7 24. Rae1 Rf8 25. g4 $14 {1-0 Zelcic,R-Cosic,R/Zadar 1998/EXT 2000 (40)}) 14... Ne5 15. Nf4 Nxd3 16. Nxd3 Bb6 17. Re1 f5 18. e5 Rad8 19. Be3 Bxe3 20. Rxe3 b6 21. Nf4 Kf7 $11 {½-½ Golubovic,B-Berebora,F/Pula 1998/EXT 2000 (36)}) (12. Bd2 Be6 13. Rfe1 Rad8 14. Be3 Bd6 15. Qxe5 Nxe5 16. Be2 f5 17. f4 Nc4 18. Bxc4 Bxc4 19. exf5 Rxf5 20. g3 Bb4 21. Red1 Re8 22. Bd4 g5 23. a3 Bxc3 24. Bxc3 gxf4 25. Rd4 Bd5 26. Rxf4 Rxf4 27. gxf4 Re2 28. Re1 Rg2+ 29. Kf1 Kf7 {½-½ Rogulj,B-Romanishin,O/Pula 1998/EXT 2000 (29)}) 12... Nxe5 {The game Nisipeanu,L-Khalifman,A/Las Vegas USA 1999 was transposed to the same position.See the game below.} 13. Be2 a5 {[%cal Ga5a4] A new move.Black's idea is to take some space on the queen side by means of a4.} (13... Bg4 14. Bxg4 Nxg4 15. h3 Nf6 16. Re1 Rfe8 17. Kf1 Bb4 18. f3 Rad8 19. Bf4 Rd7 20. Rad1 Bxc3 21. bxc3 Red8 22. Rxd7 Rxd7 23. Ke2 Kf8 24. g4 Ne8 25. h4 Nd6 26. h5 Nb5 27. Bd2 f6 28. Rg1 h6 29. Rd1 Ke7 30. Be1 Rxd1 31. Kxd1 c5 $11 {1-0 Nisipeanu,L-Khalifman,A/Las Vegas USA 1999 (59)/CBM72[Kostakiev]}) 14. Bf4 ({Immediate} 14. a4 {deserved an attention without determining the position of the bishop.}) 14... f6 15. a4 Be6 16. Rad1 Rae8 $11 {The position is about equal,but I would prefer Black as his pieces are better situated and more mobile.} 17. Nb1 {An attempt to improve position of the knight.On c3 it had no any perspectives.} Bf7 18. Nd2 Re7 19. Bxe5 $2 {[%mdl 16384] Very strange decision.Why to change a bishop?Instead White should prepare an advance f4 by means of 19.g3 and then 20.h1} (19. Bg3 $142 {[%cal Gg1h1,Gf2f4]}) 19... Rxe5 20. Bd3 Bh5 $1 21. Rde1 {[%csl Ra5][%cal Gd2c4]} Re7 $15 22. Nc4 b6 23. Nd2 $2 {[%mdl 16384] White has lost the thread.Manoeuvre c4-d2-b3 can't be considered right by any means as b3 is the most unfortunate position for the knight on the board.} (23. Kh1 $5) 23... Rd8 {[%cal Gc5b4]} 24. Nb3 Bd6 25. Bc4+ Kh8 $1 (25... Kf8 {that seems more logical allows} 26. f4 {[%cal Ge4e5] following by e5.}) 26. f3 Be8 {[%csl Ra4] looking closely at the a4-pawn.} 27. Rd1 Red7 {[%csl Rd1][%cal Gd6h2,Gd6c5]} 28. Be2 (28. Kh1 $5 $15) 28... Bf4 ({Interesting was} 28... Be5 $5 {underlining an unfortunate position of white knight.} 29. Rxd7 $8 (29. c3 $6 Rxd1 30. Rxd1 Rxd1+ 31. Bxd1 c5 (31... Bf4 32. Nd4 Bc1 33. b3 Bd2 34. Ne2 $15) 32. Nd2) 29... Rxd7 30. c3 (30. Rb1 Bf7 {[%csl Rd2]}) 30... Bf7 31. Rd1 Rd6 $1 $15 32. Nd4 $140 Bxd4+ 33. Rxd4 Bb3 {[%csl Ra4]}) 29. g3 $2 {[%mdl 8192] White doesn't feel danger.} ({The only chance to save the a4-pawn was} 29. Rxd7) (29. c3 $2 {doesn't save in view of} Be3+ 30. Kh1 Rxd1 31. Rxd1 Rxd1+ 32. Bxd1 c5 {[%csl Ra4]} 33. Na1 $140 Bc1 $19) 29... Be3+ 30. Kg2 Rxd1 31. Rxd1 Rxd1 32. Bxd1 c5 $17 {[%csl Ra4][%cal Gc5c4]} 33. f4 c4 {Black anticipates a nice end.} (33... Bxa4 $5 {is also sufficient for big advantage.} 34. Kf3 Bd4 35. Nxd4 (35. c3 Bxc3 $1 36. bxc3 c4 $19) 35... cxd4 $17) 34. Kf3 Bg1 35. Kg2 $2 {[%mdl 8192] Loses at once.} (35. Nd2 {was necessary,but after} c3 $1 36. bxc3 Bxa4 {White's chances to escape are very low.}) 35... cxb3 36. Kxg1 Bh5 $1 {[%csl Rd1][%cal Gd1c2] Nice tactical blow and a good example on the theme of overloading.} (36... Bh5 $1 37. Bxh5 bxc2 $19) 0-1

