1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 b6 3. g3 c5 4. Bg2 Bb7 5. O-O g6 6. Nc3 Bg7 7. d4 cxd4 8. Qxd4 d6 9. Rd1 Nbd7 10. Be3 (10. b3 O-O 11. Bb2 Rc8 12. Rac1 a6 (12... Rc5 $5) 13. Qd2 Rc7 14. Ne1 Bxg2 (14... Qa8 $142 15. Bxb7 Qxb7 16. Ng2 b5 $132) 15. Nxg2 Qa8 16. Ne3 Re8 17. Ncd5 Rc6 18. a4 Qb7 19. Bd4 Rcc8 20. Nxf6+ Bxf6 21. Nd5 Bxd4 22. Qxd4 Qc6 23. Qh4 f6 24. Rc3 $16 {Kramnik,V-Polgar,J/Dos Hermanas/1999/}) 10... a6 11. Rac1 Rc8 12. b3 O-O 13. Qh4 Rc7 14. Ne1 $146 {[%csl Gd5][%cal Ye1g2,Yg2f4,Yf4d5] An interesting new try, which is not as innocuous, as it seems. Compared to typical hedgehog positions with the  on e6 here the d5-square is quite vulnerable, as e6 still requires preparation. And White's e1 is aiming for d5. Illescas was possibly inspired by the abovementioned game Kramnik-J.Polgar.} (14. Bh3 Qb8 15. Bh6 b5 $1 $132 {½,Gelfand,B-Topalov,V/Batumi EU-chT/1999/}) (14. g4 $6 h6 15. h3 g5 16. Qg3 b5 $1 17. h4 bxc4 18. hxg5 hxg5 19. b4 Qa8 20. Bxg5 Re8 21. Be3 Nf8 22. a4 Ne4 23. Nxe4 Bxe4 24. Bd4 Bxf3 25. Bxf3 Qb8 26. Bd5 Qxb4 27. Bxg7 Kxg7 28. Qf4 e6 $11 {Kramnik,V-Karpov,A/Dos Hermanas/1999/}) 14... Bxg2 (14... Qa8 $5 15. Bh3 $5 {[%csl Rb6][%cal Rh3d7] d7!,a4} (15. Bxb7 Qxb7 16. Ng2 b5 17. Nf4 (17. cxb5 axb5 18. Qb4 Rb8 19. Nf4 Ne5 $11) 17... e6 $1 (17... bxc4 18. Ncd5 Nxd5 19. Nxd5 Bf6 20. Bg5 $5 $16) 18. cxb5 (18. Rxd6 b4 $1 19. Na4 Ne4 $15 {[%csl Rd6][%cal Rg6g5] g5}) 18... axb5 $36 {[%cal Rc7c3,Rf6e4,Rg6g5] c3,e4,g5}) (15. Nd5 Nxd5 16. cxd5 Bf6 17. Qb4 Rxc1 18. Bxc1 Rc8 $132)) 15. Nxg2 Re8 16. Nf4 Qb8 17. Nfd5 $14 {White has achieved his plan.} Rcc8 18. Bg5 (18. Bd4 b5 $132) (18. a4 $5 e6 19. Nxf6+ Bxf6 20. Bg5 $14) 18... Qb7 (18... b5 19. cxb5 axb5 20. Qb4 $36 {[%csl Rb5] ×b5}) 19. a4 Kh8 $1 {Moves out of the possible e7 fork.} 20. g4 {[%cal Rd1d3,Rd3h3] d3-h3} Nxd5 21. Nxd5 e6 22. Nf6 (22. Ne7 Rc7 23. Rxd6 a5 $5 24. Rcd1 Nf8 $13 {would be unclear, as White's  has no retreat and Black can capture it at the most suitable moment.}) (22. Ne3 d5 $11) 22... Nxf6 23. Bxf6 d5 $1 $11 24. Rc3 Bxf6 (24... dxc4 $4 25. Rh3 $18) 25. Qxf6+ Kg8 26. Rcd3 Qe7 {By exchanges Black has managed to ease the pressure.} 27. Qxe7 Rxe7 28. cxd5 exd5 29. Rxd5 (29. e3 Re4 30. h3 Rb4 $11) 29... Rxe2 30. Rd8+ Rxd8 31. Rxd8+ Kg7 32. Rd6 Re4 $5 ({Even the  was drawn, perhaps Black was short of time and didn't want to risk some miscalculation.} 32... Re6 33. Rxe6 fxe6 34. g5 (34. f4 e5 $1 35. fxe5 Kf7 $11) 34... e5 35. Kg2 Kf7 36. Kf3 Ke6 37. Ke4 a5 $11 {d6-e6-d6}) 33. Rxb6 Rxg4+ 34. Kf1 Rh4 (34... a5 $2 35. Rb5 $18 {[%csl Ga4,Gb3] a,b}) 35. a5 (35. Kg2 Rd4 {d3=} 36. Rxa6 Rb4 $11) 35... Rh3 $1 $11 36. b4 Rb3 37. Ke2 g5 38. Kf1 {White doesn't want to risk the consequences of the double-edged} (38. Kd2 h5 39. Kc2 $6 Rh3 $1 40. Rxa6 Rxh2 41. b5 Rxf2+ 42. Kc3 h4 (42... Rf3+ $11) 43. b6 h3 44. b7 h2 45. Rh6 $5 Rf3+ 46. Kc4 Rf4+ 47. Kc3 Kxh6 48. b8=Q Rh4 49. Qh8+ Kg6 50. Qg8+ Kf6 51. Qd8+ $11) 38... h5 39. Rxa6 Rxb4 40. Rb6 Ra4 41. a6 (41. a6 g4 $11) 1/2-1/2

