1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Be7 6. Bxf6 gxf6 7. Nf3 Nd7 $5 {This move seems to quiet risky,but it's not so clear how white may take advantage of it.} 8. Qd2 c5 (8... b6 9. d5 (9. Bb5 $5 Bb7 10. Qf4 c6 11. Bd3 Qb8 12. Qh6 Qc7 13. Qg7 Rf8 14. Qg3 O-O-O $15 {Royset,J-Djurhuus,R/NOR-chT 1997}) 9... f5 $1 10. dxe6 fxe4 11. exf7+ Kxf7 12. Qd5+ Kg7 13. Qxa8 Nc5 14. Rd1 Bd6 $44 {Stisis,Y-Zifroni,D/ISR-chT 1996}) (8... Nf8 9. O-O-O c6 10. Bc4 h5 11. h4 Qc7 12. Rhe1 Bd7 13. Nc5 $14 {½-½ Benjamin,J-Seirawan,Y/USA-ch m 1991}) (8... f5 9. Nc3 Nf6 10. O-O-O c6 11. Ne5 Bd7 12. Be2 b5 13. Bf3 Rc8 14. Kb1 $14 {Walti,R-Gast,J/SWZ-chT9697}) 9. O-O-O cxd4 (9... f5 10. Ng3 Nf6 11. Ne5 a6 12. Qh6 Qc7 13. Bc4 $36 {[%cal Gg3f5] Sievers,S-Ellers,H/BL9596}) 10. Qxd4 Qb6 11. Qa4 $5 (11. g3 $6 Qxd4 12. Nxd4 a6 $132 {[%cal Gf6f5,Gd7c5,Gc8d7]}) ({White could get symbolical advantage after} 11. Nd6+ $5 Bxd6 12. Qxd6 Qxd6 13. Rxd6 Ke7 14. Rd4 b6 15. g3 Bb7 16. Bg2 Ne5 17. Ne1 $14 {,but the draw seems to be the most likely result.}) 11... a6 12. Be2 Qc7 13. Qd4 ({Deserved attention} 13. g3 $5 f5 (13... Rb8 $5) 14. Qd4 O-O (14... e5 $2 15. Nd6+ Bxd6 16. Qxd6 Qxd6 17. Rxd6 Ke7 18. Rhd1 $16) 15. Neg5 Nf6 16. Qh4 $14 {keeping the queen on the board.}) 13... b5 14. Nd6+ {Otherwise black is just o'kay.} Bxd6 15. Qxd6 Qxd6 16. Rxd6 Bb7 17. Rhd1 Nc5 18. Ne1 $5 f5 (18... Bd5 $6 19. Bf3 $1) ({Doesn't work} 18... Ne4 $6 19. Rb6 Bd5 20. Rxa6 $1 Rxa6 21. Bxb5+ Rc6 22. Rxd5 exd5 23. Bxc6+ Ke7 24. Bxd5 $16 {and white has big advantage,if not the decisive one.}) 19. Nd3 $5 ({Another option was} 19. b4 {[%csl Rc3]} Ne4 20. Rb6 Bd5 21. Rxa6 Nc3 $1 22. Rxa8+ (22. Bxb5+ Nxb5 23. Rxd5 Rxa6 24. Rxb5 Kd7 $15) 22... Bxa8 23. Rd2 Nxa2+ 24. Kb2 Nxb4 25. Bxb5+ Ke7 26. c4 $14 {,but it seems that black should hold this endgame without problems.}) (19. Bf3 Bxf3 (19... Ne4 $6 20. Rb6 Bd5 21. Nd3 $36 {[%csl Ra6][%cal Gd3b4]}) 20. Nxf3 Ne4 21. Rb6 Nxf2 22. Rdd6 Rg8 23. g3 $13) 19... Nxd3+ (19... Ne4 $2 20. Rb6 Bd5 21. f3 Nf6 22. Nb4 $16) 20. R1xd3 Bxg2 21. Ra3 {[%csl Ra6]} Bb7 22. Rb6 O-O-O $8 (22... Bc8 23. Bxb5+ Kd8 24. Be2 Rg8 25. Rg3 Rxg3 26. hxg3 Kc7 27. Rb4 $16 {[%csl Rh7][%cal Gc2c5,Gb4h4,Gb2b4]}) 23. Rc3+ Kb8 24. Bf3 Rd7 25. Rd3 Rc7 (25... Rhd8 $2 26. Rxb7+ Rxb7 27. Rxd8+ $18) 26. Bxb7 Rxb7 27. Rxa6 $14 {Thais position is arising by force after 19.Nd3.White still keeps slightly better chanses,but with accurate play black manages to equalize.} (27. Rxb7+ $6 Kxb7 28. Rd7+ Kc6 29. Rxf7 Kd5 30. Kd2 Ke4 31. Ke2 Rc8 32. c3 b4 $1 $11) 27... Rg8 28. Rg3 Rg4 29. b3 h5 {[%cal Gh5h4]} 30. a4 bxa4 31. Rxa4 Kc7 32. f4 ({Nothing promises} 32. Kd2 $5 Rxa4 33. bxa4 Ra7 34. Ra3 Kb6 35. Kd3 Kc5 $11) 32... Kd6 33. Kd2 h4 34. Rxg4 (34. Rd3+ Ke7 35. h3 Rg2+ 36. Kd1 f6 $132) 34... fxg4 35. Ke3 f5 36. b4 Rc7 37. Kd3 g3 38. hxg3 hxg3 39. c4 g2 40. Ra6+ Rc6 41. Ra1 e5 $8 {Creating counterplay sufficient for a draw.} 42. Rg1 Ra6 $1 $11 43. Rxg2 (43. fxe5+ Kxe5 44. Rxg2 Ra3+ 45. Ke2 Rb3 $11) 43... Ra3+ 44. Ke2 exf4 45. Rg8 Rb3 46. c5+ (46. Rb8 f3+ 47. Kf2 Ke5 48. Kg3 Ke4 49. Re8+ Kd4 $11) 46... Kc7 1/2-1/2

