1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 Qc7 6. Be2 a6 7. O-O Nf6 8. Kh1 Nxd4 9. Qxd4 Bc5 10. Qd3 b5 11. f4 Bb7 12. Bf3 h5 13. Bd2 Ng4 14. Qe2 g6 {The kingside holes look ugly.} 15. Rac1 ({The point of 14...g6 is} 15. Bxg4 hxg4 16. Qxg4 b4 17. Ne2 Bxe4 {but it still looks contrived.}) 15... Rc8 16. a3 f5 17. h3 {White doesn't get carried away trying to blast open the centre to catch the black king. That would make Black's bishops work powerfully against White's own king. Instead he supports the centre and slowly pushes Black back.} Kf7 18. Rcd1 Qb6 19. Be1 Rc7 (19... Ne3 20. Rxd7+ Ke8 21. Rg7 Nxf1 22. Qxf1 {and Black's pawn structure and vulnerable king look unattractive}) 20. exf5 gxf5 21. Bxb7 Qxb7 22. Rf3 Nf6 {White has protected his position and now slowly infiltrates the weakened black position.} 23. Bh4 Ne4 24. Nxe4 Qxe4 25. Qd2 Rhc8 26. Re1 Qc6 27. Rg3 Qd6 28. Rd3 Qc6 29. Qe2 Rh8 30. Qe5 $1 Rg8 31. Qf6+ Ke8 32. Bg5 {Black is paralysed against the multiple threats of Qf6-h6-h5, Qf6-f5 and even sometimes Rxd7!? and Rxe6.} 1-0

