1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 d6 5. O-O Bg4 6. h3 h5 7. d4 b5 8. Bb3 Nxd4 9. hxg4 hxg4 10. Ng5 Nh6 {This is a funny line. Black has given a piece and White seems to be attacking, but the point of Black´s setup is the trapped  on g5.} 11. f4 (11. c3) (11. Bd5 {and}) (11. g3 {have also been played.}) 11... c6 (11... d5 $5 12. Bxd5 Bc5 13. Be3 Qd6 14. b4 Bb6 15. c4 bxc4 16. Na3 Ndf5 $13 {½-½ Ciric,D-Scholl,E/Amsterdam 1970/MCL (30)}) (11... Nxb3 12. axb3 c6 13. g3 Be7 14. c4 b4 15. Kg2 Bf6 16. Qd2 exf4 17. gxf4 Qe7 18. Re1 $14 {1-0 Rodriguez,R-Berger,B/Manila 1968/MCD (58)}) 12. g3 (12. Nxf7 $2 Qh4 13. Nxh8 g3 $19) 12... Nxb3 {This exchange seems to favour White in this line.} (12... Qe7 13. f5 (13. fxe5) 13... Qd8 14. Be3 Nxb3 15. axb3 Be7 16. Qc1 d5 $132 {0-1 Gorshkov,Y-Vorotnikov,V/Cheliabinsk 1975/MCD (30)}) 13. cxb3 exf4 14. gxf4 Qd7 15. f5 $1 $14 {Creating a nice post on e6 should Black ever consider f6. Black has two :s for the , but it´s hardly enough here.} d5 16. Bf4 O-O-O 17. Nc3 Bd6 18. Qd4 Bxf4 19. Rxf4 Qc7 20. Qf2 d4 21. Ne2 d3 22. Ng3 Kb7 23. Qe3 d2 24. Rff1 Rd7 25. Rad1 Rhd8 26. Qf4 Qb6+ 27. Rf2 Rd3 28. Kg2 $16 Qd4 29. e5 Qxb2 30. N5e4 R8d5 31. f6 Rf3 32. Rxf3 gxf3+ 33. Kxf3 Qxa2 34. fxg7 Qxb3+ 35. Ke2 Qc4+ 36. Kf2 Qd4+ 37. Kg2 1-0

