1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 g6 4. O-O Bg7 5. Re1 Nf6 6. e5 Nd5 7. Nc3 Nc7 8. Bxc6 dxc6 9. Ne4 Ne6 10. d3 O-O 11. Be3 b6 12. Qd2 f6 (12... Re8 13. Bh6 Bh8 14. c3 Ba6 15. Rad1 Qd7 16. b3 Rad8 17. c4 Bc8 18. h3 Qc7 19. Ng3 Nd4 20. Nxd4 Rxd4 21. Qe3 a5 22. f4 Bg7 23. Bxg7 Kxg7 24. Ne2 Rdd8 25. Rf1 f6 $11 {½-½ Breyther,R-Tseitlin,M/Budapest 1996/CBM 52 ext (44)}) 13. exf6 exf6 14. Bh6 a5 (14... Qd5 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 16. a4 a5 17. Rad1 Ba6 18. d4 Rad8 19. dxc5 Qxd2 20. Rxd2 Rxd2 21. Nfxd2 {½-½ Peng Xiaomin-Bu Xiangzhi/Qingdao 1999/CBM 74 no vc (21)}) 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 {This is quite a drawish variation white has chosen, while he's not risking to lose the risk for a win is not too high either.} 16. Ng3 (16. Re2 Ra7 17. Rae1 Raf7 18. h4 h5 19. b3 Qc7 20. Ng3 Nd4 21. Nxd4 cxd4 22. c3 Rd8 23. Re4 dxc3 24. Qxc3 c5 25. Ne2 Bf5 26. Nf4 Qd7 27. Ne6+ Bxe6 28. Rxe6 Qxd3 29. Qxd3 {½-½ Kramnik,V-Kasparov,G/Moscow 1996/CBM 52 ext (29)}) (16. a3 a4 17. Re2 Ra7 18. Rae1 g5 $6 19. Ng3 Nf4 20. Re4 Kg8 21. h4 $1 h6 22. Rxf4 $1 gxf4 23. Qxf4 Re7 24. Rf1 Qc7 25. Qxh6 Rh7 26. Qg6+ Rg7 27. Qe4 $16 {½-½ Karasev,V-Vasiukov,E/St Petersburg 1996/CBM 52 (60)}) (16. Qc3 Ra7 17. Rad1 Re8 18. Re3 Nd4 19. Rde1 Nb5 20. Qd2 Rae7 21. h3 Nc7 22. Ng3 Rxe3 23. fxe3 Be6 24. e4 Bf7 25. b3 Ne6 26. Ne2 Nd4 27. Nexd4 cxd4 28. Qf4 c5 29. e5 fxe5 30. Nxe5 Bd5 {½-½ Alavkin,A-Poluljahov,A/Krasnodar 1996/EXT 2000 (30)}) 16... Ra7 17. Re4 (17. h4 h5 18. Re4 Nd4 19. Nxd4 cxd4 20. Qf4 c5 21. Rae1 {The moves h4 -h5 don't make much diffference.}) 17... Nd4 18. Nxd4 cxd4 19. Qf4 (19. Rh4 Re8 20. Qh6+ Kg8 $15 {white pieces are a bit stuck on the king side which makes the position even slightly preferrable for black.}) 19... c5 20. Rae1 Raf7 21. h4 Qc7 (21... h5) 22. Qxc7 (22. Qd2 $5 f5 (22... Bb7 23. R4e2 Qc6 24. f4 $36) 23. Re8 (23. Re5 f4 24. Nf1 f3 25. g3 Qd7 $19) (23. Rf4 Re7 $15) 23... f4 24. Rxf8 Rxf8 25. Ne4 f3 26. g3 Qd7 27. Ng5 Kh8 (27... Rf6 28. Re5 $16) 28. Re6 Qc7 (28... h6 $4 29. Rxg6 Qf5 30. Rxh6+ $18) 29. Re4 $14) 22... Rxc7 {Now there are no real winning chances left for either side} 23. R4e2 (23. Re7+ Rxe7 24. Rxe7+ Rf7 25. Re8 Rc7 $11 {[%cal Gg7f7]}) 23... Kf7 24. a4 Bb7 25. b3 Rd8 26. Nf1 Rdd7 {[%cal Gd7e7]} 27. Re8 Rc8 28. R8e6 Rc6 29. Re8 Rc8 30. R8e6 1/2-1/2

